---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import SectionHead from '../components/SectionHead.astro';
import Grid from '../components/Grid.astro';
import Card from '../components/Card.astro';
import ShipStatus from '../components/ShipStatus.astro';
import RepoPill from '../components/RepoPill.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Roadmap"
  description="Attestto public roadmap. What has shipped, what is in progress, what is planned, what is under research. Every line item carries an honest ship-status label."
  lang="en"
>
  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Public roadmap</p>
      <h1>What we shipped. What we are building. What is next.</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Every line item below carries a ship-status label so adopters, grant reviewers, and pitch
        audiences can plan against verifiable state. When something moves between statuses, this
        page updates on the same commit. Nothing is labeled "shipped" until it is publicly usable.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SHIPPED -->
  <Section variant="light" id="shipped">
    <SectionHead
      label="Shipped"
      title="Available today"
      desc="Currently publicly usable. Every item below has a public repository, a public deployment, or a published specification. This is the credibility floor for grants and pitches."
    />
    <Grid cols={2}>
      <Card>
        <h3>did:sns Method Specification <ShipStatus status="shipped" /></h3>
        <p>W3C DID method anchored to Solana Name Service. Full CRUD spec, 186-test implementation report, deployed at spec.attestto.com/did-sns.</p>
        <RepoPill href="https://spec.attestto.com/did-sns/" label="spec.attestto.com/did-sns" type="spec" />
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>vLEI Solana Bridge <ShipStatus status="shipped" /></h3>
        <p>Anchor program with Groth16 zero-knowledge proofs and soulbound Program Derived Accounts. Deployed to Solana mainnet at GLEif8Rf1NFiuGPXxD7n3sakuNH6SZPFfoZMg1pBVEFm.</p>
        <RepoPill href="https://github.com/Attestto-com/vLei-Solana-Bridge" label="Attestto-com/vLei-Solana-Bridge" type="github" />
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>Verifiable Credentials SDK <ShipStatus status="shipped" /></h3>
        <p>W3C VC 2.0 SDK at attestto-com/vc-sdk. Any credential type, any DID method, Ed25519 or P-256. Costa Rica extension SDK at attestto-com/cr-vc-sdk with 11 credential types.</p>
        <RepoPill href="https://github.com/Attestto-com/vc-sdk" label="Attestto-com/vc-sdk" type="github" />
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>Credential Wallet Extension <ShipStatus status="shipped" /></h3>
        <p>Browser extension at Attestto-com/attestto-creds-extension. SD-JWT and JSON-LD VCs, DIDComm v2 messaging, Shamir 2-of-3 recovery, AES-256-GCM vault.</p>
        <RepoPill href="https://github.com/Attestto-com/attestto-creds-extension" label="Attestto-com/attestto-creds-extension" type="github" />
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>Verify Web Components <ShipStatus status="shipped" /></h3>
        <p>Drop-in JavaScript components for document verification at verify.attestto.com. Apache 2.0, no login, no backend, no data transmitted.</p>
        <RepoPill href="https://verify.attestto.com" label="verify.attestto.com" type="live" />
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>PDF Signing and Verification <ShipStatus status="shipped" /></h3>
        <p>PDF engine with PAdES-B / T / LT signing, QR embed, and Solana anchoring. Powers attestto-desktop and third-party integrations.</p>
        <RepoPill href="https://github.com/Attestto-com/attestto-verify" label="Attestto-com/attestto-verify" type="github" />
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>Attestto Anchor Service <ShipStatus status="shipped" /></h3>
        <p>Federation-ready HTTP service for anchoring content hashes to Solana via the Memo program with Merkle batching. Clone-and-deploy.</p>
        <RepoPill href="https://github.com/Attestto-com/attestto-anchor" label="Attestto-com/attestto-anchor" type="github" />
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>Trust Anchor Mirror <ShipStatus status="shipped" /></h3>
        <p>Independent public mirror of national PKI trust roots at attestto-com/attestto-trust. Costa Rica Firma Digital first, multi-country roadmap.</p>
        <RepoPill href="https://github.com/Attestto-com/attestto-trust" label="Attestto-com/attestto-trust" type="github" />
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>Attestto Desktop <ShipStatus status="shipped" /></h3>
        <p>Sovereign identity desktop application with SQLCipher-backed vault, mandatory Shamir 2-of-3 guardian recovery, offline verification.</p>
        <RepoPill href="https://github.com/Attestto-com/attestto-desktop" label="Attestto-com/attestto-desktop" type="github" />
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>DID Resolvers (did:sns, did:pki) <ShipStatus status="shipped" /></h3>
        <p>Standalone and unified DIF Universal Resolver drivers. HTTP API compliant. Deployable independently or under one service.</p>
        <RepoPill href="https://github.com/Attestto-com/attestto-did-resolver" label="Attestto-com/attestto-did-resolver" type="github" />
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>VCP CLI (Verifiable Content Provenance) <ShipStatus status="shipped" /></h3>
        <p>Embed-first content envelope CLI. Signs and verifies vcp metadata blocks inside PDF, JPEG, or a sidecar for any file. Ed25519 + JCS RFC 8785. Natural carrier for IEAL claims. Working Draft v0.1 spec + reference implementation.</p>
        <div class="card-pills">
          <RepoPill href="https://spec.attestto.com/vcp/" label="spec.attestto.com/vcp" type="spec" />
          <RepoPill href="https://github.com/Attestto-com/vcp-cli" label="Attestto-com/vcp-cli" type="github" />
        </div>
      </Card>
    </Grid>
  </Section>

  <!-- IN PROGRESS -->
  <Section variant="dark" id="in-progress">
    <SectionHead
      label="In progress"
      title="Building now (2026 H2)"
      desc="Actively under construction. Timelines are best-effort and may shift based on customer pilots or grant milestones. Nothing here is currently shippable in production."
    />
    <Grid cols={2}>
      <Card>
        <h3>IEAL Specification v0.1 <ShipStatus status="in-progress" /></h3>
        <p>Identity Evidence Assurance Level. Three-axis compositional model published as a Working Draft. Standards-community engagement at W3C CCG and DIF planned. NIST SP 800-63-4 crosswalk drafted.</p>
        <RepoPill href="https://spec.attestto.com/ieal" label="spec.attestto.com/ieal" type="spec" />
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>did:pki Method Specification <ShipStatus status="in-progress" /></h3>
        <p>W3C DID method for national PKI hierarchies. Draft v0.1.0 with active W3C DID methods registry pull request.</p>
        <RepoPill href="https://github.com/Attestto-com/did-pki-spec" label="Attestto-com/did-pki-spec" type="github" />
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>Firma Digital PKCS#11 Signing <ShipStatus status="in-progress" /></h3>
        <p>Complete the Costa Rica national signing path. Verify path is shipped; signing pipeline integrates with BCCR PKCS#11 tokens.</p>
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>PAdES-LTA with Solana Anchor <ShipStatus status="in-progress" /></h3>
        <p>Long-term archival PDF signing with Solana replacing the traditional Timestamp Authority. Embeds cert chain, DID doc snapshot, and Solana receipt in the PDF Document Security Store.</p>
        <RepoPill href="https://github.com/Attestto-com/attestto-verify" label="Attestto-com/attestto-verify" type="github" />
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>Attestto Mobile PWA <ShipStatus status="in-progress" /></h3>
        <p>Companion mobile app for camera-attested capture. Pairs with desktop via QR over local network for two-device flows.</p>
        <RepoPill href="https://github.com/Attestto-com/attestto-mobile" label="Attestto-com/attestto-mobile" type="github" />
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>Sovereign Pass SBT <ShipStatus status="in-progress" /></h3>
        <p>Non-transferable soulbound token proving verified identity after KYC. Public metadata schema at attestto-com/sovereign-pass-metadata.</p>
        <RepoPill href="https://github.com/Attestto-com/sovereign-pass-metadata" label="Attestto-com/sovereign-pass-metadata" type="github" />
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>KYC / KYB API <ShipStatus status="in-progress" /></h3>
        <p>Identity and business verification with document AI, sanctions screening, and beneficial ownership analysis. Building under CORTEX platform.</p>
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>OpenID4VP Presentation <ShipStatus status="in-progress" /></h3>
        <p>OpenID for Verifiable Presentations with selective disclosure via SD-JWT. Full offline-capable revocation status list checking in build.</p>
        <RepoPill href="https://github.com/Attestto-com/id-wallet-adapter" label="Attestto-com/id-wallet-adapter" type="github" />
      </Card>
    </Grid>
  </Section>

  <!-- PLANNED -->
  <Section variant="light" id="planned">
    <SectionHead
      label="Planned"
      title="Scheduled (2026 Q4 through 2027)"
      desc="Committed to build subject to customer or grant triggers. Nothing here is under active construction yet. Priority ordering reflects current pipeline; specific quarters may shift."
    />
    <Grid cols={2}>
      <Card>
        <h3>Play Integrity + App Attest <ShipStatus status="planned" /></h3>
        <p>Android Play Integrity API and Apple App Attest integration in attestto-mobile for hardware-attested capture. Enables IEAL Capture axis values C1 and C2. Priority P2 per IEAL implementation roadmap.</p>
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>PAD Vendor Integrations <ShipStatus status="planned" /></h3>
        <p>ISO/IEC 30107-3 certified PAD provider integrations for IEAL Algorithm axis values A3 and A4. Customer-triggered per vendor-neutrality policy. Mitek, iProov, FaceTec are candidate integrations.</p>
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>.attestto Container Format <ShipStatus status="planned" /></h3>
        <p>File envelope carrying encrypted witnesses, VC commitments, attestation blobs, and access-control policies for institutional dual storage. Design ADR pending, follow-on to IEAL v0.1.</p>
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>Multi-stablecoin Treasury Rails <ShipStatus status="planned" /></h3>
        <p>Stablecoin-agnostic treasury infrastructure. USDC and EURC via Circle CCTP, USDG via the Global Dollar Network, and OUSD (Open Standard consortium, Solana-native, launching late 2026) as it matures. Rail selection follows regional partner and merchant preference, not vendor lock-in. Organization-scoped, governance-approval-gated, settlement batching supported.</p>
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>Squads Multisig Vaults <ShipStatus status="planned" /></h3>
        <p>Product-level governance multisig on Solana Squads v4. 2-of-3 or custom thresholds for domain, asset, and signing-key custody.</p>
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>LEI Issuance and Maintenance <ShipStatus status="planned" /></h3>
        <p>Legal Entity Identifier issuance and annual maintenance for Attestto Inc.'s own entity chain first, then a public issuance service. GLEIF-compatible under vLEI framework.</p>
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>Colegio and Notary Onboarding Kit <ShipStatus status="planned" /></h3>
        <p>Turn-key onboarding for Costa Rica professional colegios (bar, medical, engineering) and notary offices. Ties professional-attestation model to Firma Digital signing.</p>
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>Digital Currency Rails (CRCD) <ShipStatus status="planned" /></h3>
        <p>Stablecoin on-ramp, off-ramp, and cross-border settlement. Costa Rica digital colón (CRCD) proof of concept depends on BCCR partnership timelines.</p>
      </Card>
    </Grid>
  </Section>

  <!-- RESEARCH -->
  <Section variant="dark" id="research">
    <SectionHead
      label="Research"
      title="Under exploration (2027+)"
      desc="Long-horizon research items with no build commitment. Included for transparency about where we think the space is heading. Priority is guided by standards-community direction and customer signals."
    />
    <Grid cols={3}>
      <Card>
        <h3>Post-Quantum Signing <ShipStatus status="research" /></h3>
        <p>ML-DSA-65 hybrid signing (NIST FIPS 204). Migration path documented. Shipping target aligned with the industry 2030 timeline for post-quantum readiness.</p>
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>Zero-Knowledge Predicates <ShipStatus status="research" /></h3>
        <p>Range proofs and set-membership proofs in OpenID4VP presentations. Depends on standardization progress and mobile ZK proving performance.</p>
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>Session-Based IEAL <ShipStatus status="research" /></h3>
        <p>Extending IEAL from single-capture to session-based continuous assurance. Applicable to remote proctoring, multi-party signing ceremonies, and long-lived KYC sessions.</p>
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>Cross-Jurisdiction Issuer Registry <ShipStatus status="research" /></h3>
        <p>ToIP Trust Registry Protocol implementation for cross-jurisdiction issuer discovery and trust chain composition. Aligns with HAVID.</p>
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>AI-Mediated Onboarding <ShipStatus status="research" /></h3>
        <p>Conversational identity provisioning with on-device LLMs. Consciousness Shards architecture. Governed by per-event consent per IEAL Storage axis.</p>
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>On-Chain Cap Table <ShipStatus status="research" /></h3>
        <p>Regulatory-cleared on-chain equity structures. Blocked on securities-law clarity across LATAM jurisdictions. Watching but not building.</p>
      </Card>
    </Grid>
  </Section>

  <!-- STANDARDS ENGAGEMENT -->
  <Section variant="light" id="standards-engagement">
    <SectionHead
      label="Standards engagement"
      title="Where we participate"
      desc="Standards work is core to Attestto's positioning. Publishing specifications and engaging peer standards bodies is not a marketing tactic; it is how the identity infrastructure category matures. Below is our current engagement track."
    />
    <Grid cols={2}>
      <Card>
        <h3>W3C Credentials Community Group <ShipStatus status="in-progress" /></h3>
        <p>Active engagement on did:pki registry, did:sns discussion, IEAL peer review, and related identity primitives.</p>
        <RepoPill href="https://w3c-ccg.github.io/" label="w3c-ccg.github.io" type="ext" />
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>Decentralized Identity Foundation (DIF) <ShipStatus status="in-progress" /></h3>
        <p>HAVID alignment via peer discussion. IEAL scope introduced as a compositional identity assurance model for DIF adopters.</p>
        <RepoPill href="https://identity.foundation/" label="identity.foundation" type="ext" />
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>NIST SP 800-63-4 <ShipStatus status="planned" /></h3>
        <p>NIST 800-63-4 was finalized 2025-07-31. When NIST opens a future revision comment window, IEAL will be part of our submission. Meanwhile we publish an informative crosswalk.</p>
        <RepoPill href="https://pages.nist.gov/800-63-4/" label="pages.nist.gov/800-63-4" type="ext" />
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>ToIP Trust Registry Protocol <ShipStatus status="research" /></h3>
        <p>Watching HAVID and TRP developments for interoperability with our federated trust bootstrap model. Long-term direction depends on ToIP publication cadence.</p>
        <RepoPill href="https://trustoverip.org/" label="trustoverip.org" type="ext" />
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>GLEIF vLEI Framework <ShipStatus status="shipped" /></h3>
        <p>vLEI Solana Bridge deployed as an on-chain implementation of the GLEIF vLEI Framework. Attestto Inc. LEI issuance and maintenance planned as a follow-on service.</p>
        <RepoPill href="https://www.gleif.org/en/vlei/introducing-the-vlei-ecosystem-governance-framework" label="gleif.org/vlei" type="ext" />
      </Card>
      <Card>
        <h3>OpenID Foundation (OIDF) <ShipStatus status="planned" /></h3>
        <p>OpenID4VP and OpenID4VC implementer conformance. Attestto's presentation flow targets full HAIP 1.0 alignment.</p>
        <RepoPill href="https://openid.net/wg/digital-credentials-protocols/" label="openid.net/wg/dcp" type="ext" />
      </Card>
    </Grid>
  </Section>

  <!-- LEGEND -->
  <Section variant="plain">
    <div class="legend">
      <h2>How to read this roadmap</h2>
      <ul class="legend-list">
        <li>
          <ShipStatus status="shipped" />
          <span><strong>Shipped</strong>: publicly usable today. Has a public repository, deployment, or published specification.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <ShipStatus status="in-progress" />
          <span><strong>In progress</strong>: under active construction. Timelines are best-effort. Not shippable in production yet.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <ShipStatus status="planned" />
          <span><strong>Planned</strong>: committed subject to customer, grant, or pilot trigger. Not under active construction.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <ShipStatus status="research" />
          <span><strong>Research</strong>: exploratory. No build commitment. Included for transparency about long-horizon direction.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="legend-note">
        This roadmap is honest about ship status because we would rather ship credibility over hype.
        A category-defining specification is worth more than a coming-soon claim. If a line item is
        important to your evaluation, ask us for the current state.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding-block: var(--space-xl) var(--space-lg);
    background: var(--color-dark);
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  .hero .eyebrow {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs-size);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-dark-sky);
    margin-block-end: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .hero h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-hero-size);
    font-weight: 800;
    line-height: var(--text-hero-line);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    color: #ffffff;
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  .hero .lead {
    font-size: var(--text-body-lg-size);
    color: var(--text-on-dark-muted);
    max-width: 45rem;
    margin-block-start: var(--space-md);
    line-height: var(--text-body-lg-line);
  }

  .card-pills {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-block-start: auto;
    padding-block-start: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .legend {
    max-width: 42rem;
  }

  .legend h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-h3-size);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-block-end: var(--space-md);
  }

  .legend-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .legend-list li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .legend-list strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .legend-note {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-md);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-small-size);
    line-height: 1.6;
    font-style: italic;
  }
</style>
